hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16311","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: I was informed that Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, and from Sulayman ibn Musa, from so-and-so, and from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, and Abu al-Zubayr did not attain all this story, that Abu Qatadah came to his family and found a bowl of tharid made of sacrificial jerky, and he refused to eat it, so he came to Qatadah ibn al-Nu'man and informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood in Hajj and said: I had commanded you not to eat the sacrifices beyond three days so that it suffices you, and indeed I permit it for you, so eat of it as you wish. He said: And do not sell the meat of the sacrificial animals and the sacrifices, so eat and give charity and benefit from their skins, and if you are fed anything of its meat, then eat it if you wish."
"16312","He said: Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to me, he said: Sulayman ibn Musa said: Zubayd informed me, that Abu Sa'id al-Khudri came to his family and found a bowl of sacrificial jerky, and he refused to eat it, so he came to Qatadah ibn al-Nu'man and informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and said: I had commanded you not to eat the sacrifices beyond three days so that it suffices you, and indeed I permit it for you, so eat of it as you wish, and do not sell the meat of the sacrificial animals and the sacrifices, so eat and give charity and benefit from their skins, and do not sell them, and if you are fed of its meat, then eat if you wish. And he said in this hadith, from Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): So now eat and trade and store."
"16313","Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me, from Jabir, similar to this hadith of Zubayd, from Abu Sa'id; all that did not reach him from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"16314","He said: Abd al-Malik ibn 'Amr narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, from Sharik, meaning Ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Namir Tamim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'id al-Khudri, from his father and his uncle Qatadah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat the meat of the sacrifices and store."
"16315","He said: Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Husayn ibn Ja'far and my father Ishaq ibn Yasar narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Khabbab, freedman of Banu 'Adi ibn al-Najjar, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had forbidden us to eat the meat of our sacrifices beyond three. He said: So I went out on a journey, then I came to my family, and that was after al-Adha by days. He said: So my wife brought me a leg in which she had put jerky. So I said to her: Whence do you have this jerky? So she said: From our sacrifices. He said: So I said to her: Did not the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid us to eat it beyond three? He said: So she said: Indeed he has given license to the people after that. He said: So I did not believe her until I sent to my brother Qatadah ibn al-Nu'man, and he was a Badri, asking him about that. He said: So he sent to me: Eat your food, for she has told the truth; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has given license to the Muslims concerning that."
